        <item>
            <title>3.14.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:29:50 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>182</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.14.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- **Idle sessions stay in Open.** The session service used to stop a session nobody was watching after 15 minutes and move its row to Recents. The limit is now a setting, "Stop idle sessions after" (4 hours by default, or Never), and a stopped session keeps its row in Open. Click it to resume.
- **Click the cup in the sidebar footer** to turn "Prevent sleep while working" on and off. The icon shows three states: held awake, not held awake, and off.
- **Control API: know why a turn or a session ended.**
  - `turn_done` now carries `isError`, plus `errorKind` and `errorCode` when the turn failed (rate limit, login, network and so on).
  - `session_closed` carries a `reason`.
  - A new `turn_interrupted` event reports a turn that was stopped, crashed, or cut off by a restart. Canopy never resends it.
- **Control API: keep working across an update.**
  - After the session service restarts for an update, sessions opened through `open_session` come back under the same key.
  - A `listen` cursor from before the restart continues with no gap.
- **`canopyctl listen --follow`** keeps listening, prints one line per event, and reconnects on its own. `--cursor-file` remembers the position between runs.
- **A session opened through the control API is not stopped for being idle while a client is listening to it.**

### Bug Fixes
- With the sidebar collapsed, the leftmost pane's header ignored most clicks (right-click menu, close button, double-click rename, click to focus). It responds again.
]]></description>
